+## JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7396)
+
+```ts
+import { applyMergePatch } from "./src/index.ts";
+
+applyMergePatch({ a: "b", c: { d: "e", f: "g" } }, { a: "z", c: { f: null } }); // { a: "z", c: { d: "e" } }
+```
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)` implements the MergePatch algorithm of RFC 7396 §2 and returns the result as a
+new value; neither argument is mutated and the result shares no structure with them. An object patch is merged
+into the target recursively (a non-object target is treated as `{}`): a `null` member removes that member (a
+no-op if absent), any other value is merged into the target's member of the same name, and members the patch
+does not name are kept. A patch that is not an object (array, string, number, boolean or `null`) replaces the
+target as a whole, so arrays are never merged element-wise and a top-level `null` patch yields `null`; `null`
+inside a replacing array is kept. It throws a `JsonMergePatchError` if `target` or `patch` contains, at any
+depth, something that is not a JSON value (`undefined`, a function, a symbol, a bigint or a non-finite number).
+Only own members of the target are considered, and members named `__proto__` are handled as ordinary data.
+
 Tests: `npm test`.
